WEBVTT

00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:17,010
In the 1980s, I heard about colostrum being used to combat cancer, is that still being used?

00:00:19,330 --> 00:00:27,570
No, there are some cancers that don't do well with colostrum. I actually wrote an article about this

00:00:27,570 --> 00:00:34,770
if you search the blog for colostrum and cancer. I think that's what the title of the article is called.

00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:43,090
But it just talks about the pros and cons of colostrum. Usually I say most cancer patients don't

00:00:43,090 --> 00:00:48,450
have a problem using colostrum. They want to help with their hair or their nails or something like

00:00:48,450 --> 00:00:57,090
that, but it's not considered at all a cancer treatment any longer. There's pros and cons to

00:00:57,090 --> 00:01:04,530
colostrum. It can accelerate growth in some cancers and there's some data that it can help with

00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:13,010
people with cancer. So there's a lot of mixed data about colostrum out there. And I don't think it's

00:01:14,210 --> 00:01:18,210
you know, there's a lot of data that's out there that's very biased, but I don't think it's unbiased.

00:01:18,210 --> 00:01:24,770
I don't think it's biased. I think there's cause to be concerned about using excess colostrum

00:01:24,770 --> 00:01:33,090
with cancer patients, especially if it's an epithelial cell cancer, like a colon cancer or something

00:01:33,090 --> 00:01:37,730
like that. If a person had a lymphoma or something, I don't think there's any harm in using colostrum.

00:01:39,570 --> 00:01:48,610
But you could check out that article on our blog.

